  "indias-two-tracks-of-health-cover-and": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Urban_Primary_Health_Centre_Ayushman_Bharat_Bidipeth_Nagpur.jpg/960px-Urban_Primary_Health_Centre_Ayushman_Bharat_Bidipeth_Nagpur.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"People queuing outside an Ayushman Bharat urban primary health centre in Nagpur\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">An Ayushman Bharat primary health centre in Nagpur — the public-scheme side of India's two parallel, and largely complementary, tracks of health cover. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Urban_Primary_Health_Centre_Ayushman_Bharat_Bidipeth_Nagpur.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Urban Primary Health Centre Ayushman Bharat Bidipeth Nagpur.jpg</a>, Ganesh Dhamodkar, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
